// expect: 10
// A declaration's instance is a fact the run keeps: `lfo` declares 750 Hz
// and reaches its rate through a stage that names no instance, so that
// stage runs at 750 Hz and its perform passes the 48 kHz clock to the one
// serving 750. On boot 342695ce the stage's perform reached the innermost
// clock by the effect's name, and `lfo` read 48000 under a declaration
// that said 750 — a false proof of the row it published.
import dsp/clock

fn stage() = sample_rate()

fn lfo() with Sample(750) = stage()

fn main() = lfo() - 740 ~> sample_at(48000) ~> sample_at(750)
